    "summary": "Concha belt composed of fourteen component parts mounted on leather. There are six oval, domed shapes made of coin silver, with scalloped edges and with a radiating repoussé design, stamped with a central oval turquoise. The butterfly shapes are symmetrical and three prongs made by repoussé and with a central oval turquoise. There are seven of these interspersing the oval shapes. The buckle is rectangular in shape with six square turquoise and appears to be by a different maker. The turquoise seem to have been added on later as the stamping on the buckle goes underneath the bezels.",
